{"name":"Mint Leaves","hex":"#6a7d4e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mint","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A building or institution where money (originally, only coins) is produced under government licence.","A vast sum of money;  a large amount of something."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To reproduce (coins), usually en masse, under licence.","To invent; to forge; to fabricate; to fashion."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mint"},{"term":"leaves","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of leaf","from leave:\nplural of leave \nplural of leave"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of leave"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leaves"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mentha","blocks":[{"text":"Mentha, also known as mint, is a genus of flowering plants in the mint family, Lamiaceae. It is estimated that 18 to 24 species exist, but the exact distinction between species is unclear. Hybridization occurs naturally where some species' ranges overlap. Many hybrids and cultivars are known."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Mentha_spicata-IMG_6186.jpg/330px-Mentha_spicata-IMG_6186.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mentha","wikidata":"Q47859"},{"title":"Leaf","blocks":[{"text":"A leaf is a principal appendage of the stem of a vascular plant, usually borne laterally above ground and specialized for photosynthesis. Leaves are collectively called foliage, as in \"autumn foliage\", while the leaves, stem, flower, and fruit collectively form the shoot system. In most leaves, the primary photosynthetic tissue is the palisade mesophyll and is located on the upper side of the blade or lamina of the leaf, but in some species, including the mature foliage of Eucalyptus, palisade mesophyll is present on both sides and the leaves are said to be isobilateral. The leaf is an integral part of the stem system, and most leaves are flattened and have distinct upper (adaxial) and lower (abaxial) surfaces that differ in color, hairiness, the number of stomata, the amount and structure of epicuticular wax, and other features. Leaves are mostly green in color due to the presence of a compound called chlorophyll, which is essential for photosynthesis as it absorbs light energy from the Sun. A leaf with lighter-colored or white patches or edges is called a variegated leaf."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Lisc_lipy.jpg/330px-Lisc_lipy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leaf","wikidata":"Q33971"},{"title":"Spring green","blocks":[{"text":"Spring green is a color that was traditionally considered to be on the yellow side of green, but in modern computer systems based on the RGB color model is halfway between cyan and green on the color wheel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/%D0%97%D2%AF%D0%BC%D1%96%D1%80%D0%B5%D1%82.jpg/330px-%D0%97%D2%AF%D0%BC%D1%96%D1%80%D0%B5%D1%82.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_green","wikidata":"Q373787"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Mentha_piperita_-_Flickr_-_aspidoscelis_%281%29.jpg/500px-Mentha_piperita_-_Flickr_-_aspidoscelis_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Mentha_piperita_-_Flickr_-_aspidoscelis_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Mentha_piperita_-_Flickr_-_aspidoscelis_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Mentha_piperita_-_Flickr_-_aspidoscelis_%281%29.jpg/500px-Mentha_piperita_-_Flickr_-_aspidoscelis_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=e